                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What makes men's grooming agency different from women's beauty agency?</h3>
                                        <p>Different creator network (streetwear + lifestyle + fitness vs beauty-creator), different creative style (masculine + minimalist vs feminine + luxury), different channel mix (Meta + Instagram + Reels dominant, LinkedIn light-touch for B2B gift), different content (grooming + beard + skincare-for-men vs women's concern-content).</p>
                                        <h3>What sub-vertical positioning wins in men's grooming?</h3>
                                        <p>Premium + streetwear-adjacent (Bombay Shaving), beard specialist (Beardo), ayurveda + herbal (Ustraa + The Man Company), wellness + performance (Man Matters), sensory + fragrance-first (emerging), clinical + concern-solving (under-served). Pick ONE + own it year 1.</p>
                                        <h3>What agency capabilities matter for men's grooming?</h3>
                                        <p>Named client work + streetwear-adjacent + lifestyle + fitness creator network + masculine + minimalist creative + Meta + Instagram + Reels funnel + LinkedIn light-touch + subscription + concern + tutorial + lifestyle content.</p>
                                        <h3>Is men's grooming easier to launch than women's skincare?</h3>
                                        <p>Faster launch cycles (5-30 days vs 30-90 for women's) + higher trial-and-repeat + faster payback. Under-served with 40-50% YoY growth = white-space opportunity. But subscription programme + retention less mature than women's.</p>
                                        <h3>What creator network works for men's grooming?</h3>
                                        <p>Streetwear + lifestyle + fitness + gaming + entrepreneur + men's-focused creator vs beauty-creator women's. Micro (10-100K) best ROI tier. Bombay Shaving + Beardo + Man Matters partnerships with lifestyle + fitness + finfluencer + entrepreneur-adjacent creators.</p>
                                        <h3>What is realistic launch envelope for men's grooming D2C?</h3>
                                        <p>Rs 25-60L boutique. Rs 50-90L mid-market. Rs 90+L premium + full-range. Lower capex than premium ayurveda + clean beauty due to faster payback + smaller inventory. Revenue Rs 20-70L / month by month 12 for well-executed.</p>
                                        <h3>Should we launch as beard-specialist or full-range grooming?</h3>
                                        <p>Beard-specialist or single-sub-category (shave OR beard OR face OR fragrance) at launch. Own it year 1 + expand adjacent year 2-3. Bombay Shaving started shaving + expanded. Full-range at launch dilutes.</p>
